<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4948] Web session clustering fails to work with Spring Security</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4948</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;WebSessionFilter.doFilterV2&lt;/tt&gt; method do not refresh the local instance of session after &lt;tt&gt;chain.doFilter&lt;/tt&gt;. But it&apos;s possible that session is replaced by some other filter (e.g. due to login). And if after this replacement some attributes are added, they do not end up in cache.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;dev@ list discussion: &lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/IGNITE-2741-spring-session-design-td14560.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/IGNITE-2741-spring-session-design-td14560.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
